diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
index e92768b..1452500 100644
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ Screen sharing is built on top of the voice connections. The person sharing pick
 
 The person sharing chooses one of four quality levels: 720p at 15 frames per second (the default), 720p at 30, 1080p at 15 and 1080p at 30. The preference for smooth motion or sharp text is passed to the browser as a content hint. The share audio is always requested, and whether it is shared is chosen only in the source picker (the audio option in the browser's picker, or the box in the desktop app's own picker). If the browser provides tab or system audio, it is sent as a track separate from the microphone, otherwise the share continues with video only. The audio is requested with the `restrictOwnAudio` constraint: a browser that supports it and the desktop app remove the sounds Telsiz itself plays (the conversation, notification sounds, Telsiz DJ) from the system audio, so listeners do not hear their own voices back through the share. On older Windows versions that do not support this separation, all system audio is shared. In a full mesh, the upload bandwidth of the person sharing is used separately for each viewer. In the desktop app, the app's own screen and window picker opens instead of the browser picker.
 
-The person sharing can minimize the preview (`22-cast.js`): the stage closes, while sharing and the video sent to viewers continue, and Show Preview appears in the chip in the top bar. The choice is kept on the device in `telsiz.castOwnMin`, and on a narrow screen the preview is always visible because the top bar has no chip there. The Floating Window button in the stage header opens the room and a Stop button for the person sharing (a preview of their own screen would create a mirror effect), and the watched stream for a viewer, in a floating window (see Floating window).
+The person sharing can minimize the preview (`22-cast.js`): the stage closes, while sharing and the video sent to viewers continue, and Show Preview appears in the chip in the top bar. The choice is kept on the device in `telsiz.castOwnMin`, and on a narrow screen the preview is always visible because the top bar has no chip there. The Floating Window button in the stage header opens the room and a Stop button for the person sharing (a preview of their own screen would create a mirror effect), and the watched stream for a viewer, in a floating window (see Floating window). For the person sharing, the preview is minimized only for that share and the saved choice does not change.
 
